{"parentUuid":"7adb0641-ae9b-44c8-bb49-f8d56ebba41b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"13b2e94d-1b2a-4672-944b-f2e4cd21284b","agentId":"a2f342f6277bc9475","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015bJXaheJiAwyfRtJtFjzdN","type":"tool_result","content":"107:- Prilepin's chart (total reps and reps-per-set by %1RM) is the default guide for daily rep/set assignment within a training block, used consistently across strength and power teaching. **Inferred/Explicit (shared team material)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.19; hhpr-5355-class-8-2026.md p.15] Inference: with no true 1RM testing (Q10), any %1RM prescription rests on projected maxes. Kept on that explicit basis (Tension 16, resolved 2026-10-02).\n\nNew tensions raised by the interview (2026-09-28):\n\n11. **Eric's own slide against his interview on residual effects.** The class-4 slide (p. 47), from a session Eric taught, says aerobic fitness is lost fastest and speed slowest. In the interview he s\n12. **Daily mRSI testing against a Wednesday read.** The SportSmith piece describes mRSI from daily CMJ testing as the daily readiness marker [2026-02-19-sportsmith-6otb-er.md]. Q2 names Wednesday as \n    **Status: RESOLVED 2026-10-02 (Eric).** Daily jumps are collected to build the rolling baseline and SWC; Wednesday is the single decision read that changes the week.\n13. **\"We don't assess readiness\" against mRSI as the readiness marker.** Q22 says Applied Performance does not assess readiness in RTP; the SportSmith piece and Q2 describe mRSI readiness reads. Infe\n14. **\"Support\" role against \"it doesn't really end\".** The Playbook frames RTP input as support to Athletic Medicine and Athletic Performance decisions [baylor-applied-performance-playbook.md p.6]. Q\n15. **The Q3 rule against current practice.** Eric's rule is that a test with no question or need has no place (Q3). Yet ACWR is still looked at (\"We dabble with ACWR\") though he does not \"trust it fo\n16. **No true 1RM against %1RM prescription.** No sport tests true 1RM (Q10), while Prilepin's chart and the phase bands are written in %1RM [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.19; week1-lecture.m","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5414a8c2-9291-4b0e-9387-2577b6017812","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:05:03.784Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"107:- Prilepin's chart (total reps and reps-per-set by %1RM) is the default guide for daily rep/set assignment within a training block, used consistently across strength and power teaching. **Inferred/Explicit (shared team material)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.19; hhpr-5355-class-8-2026.md p.15] Inference: with no true 1RM testing (Q10), any %1RM prescription rests on projected maxes. Kept on that explicit basis (Tension 16, resolved 2026-10-02).\n\nNew tensions raised by the interview (2026-09-28):\n\n11. **Eric's own slide against his interview on residual effects.** The class-4 slide (p. 47), from a session Eric taught, says aerobic fitness is lost fastest and speed slowest. In the interview he s\n12. **Daily mRSI testing against a Wednesday read.** The SportSmith piece describes mRSI from daily CMJ testing as the daily readiness marker [2026-02-19-sportsmith-6otb-er.md]. Q2 names Wednesday as \n    **Status: RESOLVED 2026-10-02 (Eric).** Daily jumps are collected to build the rolling baseline and SWC; Wednesday is the single decision read that changes the week.\n13. **\"We don't assess readiness\" against mRSI as the readiness marker.** Q22 says Applied Performance does not assess readiness in RTP; the SportSmith piece and Q2 describe mRSI readiness reads. Infe\n14. **\"Support\" role against \"it doesn't really end\".** The Playbook frames RTP input as support to Athletic Medicine and Athletic Performance decisions [baylor-applied-performance-playbook.md p.6]. Q\n15. **The Q3 rule against current practice.** Eric's rule is that a test with no question or need has no place (Q3). Yet ACWR is still looked at (\"We dabble with ACWR\") though he does not \"trust it fo\n16. **No true 1RM against %1RM prescription.** No sport tests true 1RM (Q10), while Prilepin's chart and the phase bands are written in %1RM [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.19; week1-lecture.m","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7adb0641-ae9b-44c8-bb49-f8d56ebba41b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
