alized-\n== claim--strength-training-threshold-stimulus econdBrain/Knowledge\n    Separately, Korobkov, Gerasimov & Vasiliev (via Verkhoshansky, 1977) are cited for the\n    Vasiliev via Verkhoshansky 1977; PDF pp. 33-34, printed pp. 22-23). **Inference:** do no\n== claim--velocity-and-contraction-specificity-asymmetric-transfer econdBrain/Knowledge\n    # High-Velocity Training Transfers to Low Velocity Better Than the Reverse; Contraction Modes B\n    high-velocity strength; high-velocity isokinetic training improves high-velocity strength\n    target quality, not default to high velocity in every case. **Eric's baseline:**\n== principle--training-effort-must-match-or-exceed-sport-effort-judged-by-movement-speed econdBrain/Knowledge\n    chapter: \"4.3.3\"\n== claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence econdBrain/Knowledge\n    chapter: \"4.3.1\"\n== principle--force-time-profile-determines-strength-vs-power-training-target econdBrain/Knowledge\n    chapter: \"2.2.2\"\n    **What it is** — The authors illustrate with a thought experiment (Fig 2.14-2.15): two","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0439f920-e760-4356-9163-1e5032fc3df2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
