{"parentUuid":"41679a71-19e1-495a-817b-12172f9e6fe6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2f342f6277bc9475","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffbdrdy7Y2emSQCBiBBf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Overall verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** Of the 19 entries, 11 are GO, 8 need fixes and none are NO-GO.\n\nI checked every equation, table, figure and number against page images I rendered and opened myself. That covered PDF idx 266-278. All the \"Eric's baseline:\" quotes and line numbers match `method-baseline.md`, and every wikilink points to a real file. No entry repeats an existing vault or staging entry without adding something new.\n\n**The areas you flagged:**\n- **The `proven` entry (Newton II / impulse):** keeping it `proven` is right, because the scope is limited to the impulse-momentum identity. Three of its own physics sentences are imprecise, so it gets a FIX (items 1-3 under Newton II below).\n- **The two `contested` entries (three maximum-strength methods; APRE):** both sides of every contradiction are on the cited pages.\n- **Load-to-reps numbers:** 89% for the 5RM (printed 258), 90-95% with 3-6 reps (261) and 85-95% for 3-5RM (260) all match the pages.\n- **Tables 5.1, 5.2, 5.3 and Fig 5.4:** every cell matches the page image.\n\n**Required fixes, one line:**\n\n**Newton II:**\n1. The book's ΔV is the final velocity, so m.ΔV equals the change in momentum only when the body starts from rest.\n2. Write \"net propulsive impulse\" (ground force minus body weight), not \"propulsive impulse\".\n3. Replace the circular-motion example with a projectile under constant gravity, and write \"net external force on the body\".\n\n**Dynamic correspondence:**\n4. The neuromuscular paragraph *closes* the dynamics discussion (after Fig 5.1); it does not come before it.\n5. Label the \"This passage is... Use it when\" sentence as Inference.\n\n**Three methods:**\n6. Name which pairing actually clashes: 90-95% with 3-6 reps clearly conflicts with 5RM = 89%; 85-95% = 3-5RM is only loosely off.\n7. Rewrite the line-105 sentence fragment with an \"Eric's baseline:\" prefix.\n\n**DeLorme:**\n8. \"Mostly in rehabilitation or untrained subjects\" is not on the page; remove it or label it Inference.\n\n**Berger:**\n9. Two of the six conclusions do trace to the Berger 1963 sentences on printed 259 (conclusion 1's comparator and conclusion 5). Conclusion 3 traces loosely, and only conclusion 6 has no data on the page.\n10. Add the printed-259 sentence that advanced weightlifters train mostly at 1-3 reps.\n\n**Ivanov:**\n11. Retitle and rename. The title \"each improves its own test\" does not fit the data: eccentric training had no eccentric test and raised the squat 1RM most.\n12. Label the \"trains the nervous system for that mode\" gloss as Inference.\n\n**Implement mass:**\n13. Retitle and rename away from \"stay close to competition mass\". That is Bondarchuk's view; this book's own examples include a 3 kg javelin training weight, 2 kg vs 4 kg medicine balls, a 0.6-0.8 kg puck and 2 kg bats. The page's actual rule is keeping technique intact and sizing the heavy implement per athlete.\n\n**After the renames:**\n14. Update the one inbound link to each renamed file: Ivanov from the three-methods entry, implement mass from the speed-strength loading entry.\n\nTwo small gaps can go into existing entries rather than new ones: the 1-3 rep sentence (item 10) and the section's two-lever summary for speed-strength (after-effect plus inertia). The report also lists three suggested two-way links to the 5b/5c entries.\n\nReport: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":219526,"output_tokens":1313,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":637},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1313,"cache_read_input_tokens":219526,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":637,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffbdPxcWPJe2D147njgY","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"54a009db-ecf1-4cb6-b413-67305b7ea1db","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:12:23.565Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
